        "original_id": "2254b335-0487-519e-af93-466a87a0b2c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Furst, H. P. Lovecraft, Eric Ambler, Graham Greene, Joseph Roth, Arthur Koestler\n- Products: The Polish Officer\n- Topics: historical spy novels, horror fiction, literary influences\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was an American author born on August 20, 1890, who later became posthumously famous for influential works of horror fiction.\n- H. P. Lovecraft died on March 15, 1937.\n- Alan Furst was born on February 20, 1941, and he is an American author of historical spy novels.\n- Alan Furst has been described as an heir to the tradition of Eric Ambler and Graham Greene.\n- Alan Furst cited Eric Ambler, Graham Greene, Joseph Roth, and Arthur Koestler as important influences.\n- The Polish Officer, published in 1995, is a novel by Alan Furst.",
